WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.601
-Mikey Day,
it is great to see you.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.968
You know I'm a fan of yours.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:05.000
You look great in a suit, buddy.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.267
I never really see you
in a suit.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:07.300
-Aw, thanks.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.968
-Here you are,
season six on "SNL."

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:10.334
-Yeah.

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:12.000
-And crushing it as a cast
member as well as a writer.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.968
-So nice of you.
-You're great.

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:17.300
Do you find yourself,
after six seasons,

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.234
still star-struck
sometimes or...?

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:20.734
-Yeah, occasionally.

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:23.767
It's usually people
who are at a taping

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:26.133
that you don't know
are going to be there.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:29.100
The one interaction I had that
was, like --

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:35.234
I still think about,
in that I -- it was so awkward.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:39.834
I was -- It was the season
finale on my first season

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:44.400
as a cast member,
and they were setting up the set

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.100
for a sketch that took place on
"Jurassic Park: The Ride."

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.367
And I played someone
who worked on the ride.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:56.367
So I had a khaki shirt with
the Jurassic Park logo on it.

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:59.701
And I'm just standing there,
and I hear someone say,

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:01.000
"Hey, I know that."

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.033
And I look
and it's Steven Spielberg...

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:05.334
[ Laughter ]
...who, like --

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:07.834
I grew up a Spielberg kid,
I mean,

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:11.634
so instrumental
in my upbringing.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:15.634
So, to go from zero
to Steven Spielberg --

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:16.901
You're like...
-Yeah.

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:18.868
And what did you say?
-I said --

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:21.834
And I don't know why
this came out of my mouth.

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:24.234
And I think about it
every once in a while

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:26.434
alone and just start cringing.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:29.467
He goes, "I know that,"
and is pointing at the logo.

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:33.167
And I said, "Yeah, the sketch
doesn't take place

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:36.234
in the actual park.
It takes place on the ride."

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:40.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:42.200
Why? Dude!
-Wow, wow.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.934
-Dude!
-Wow.

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:46.200
-That's so weird.
Why did I -- I don't know why.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.267
-That's too much detail.
What did he do?

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:51.801
-He didn't say, "Hey, does this
take place in the actual park?"

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:53.634
"Oh, no, it takes place
on the ride."

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:57.133
-No, but how do you that react
to that as any human being?

00:01:57.133 --> 00:02:01.767
-I recall him just, like,
smiling like a normal person

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:04.234
would and then
kind of walking away.

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:08.534
And I thought about it
for so long.

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:10.567
It's so dumb. What?

00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:13.000
-What if you went back in time,
and could say something?

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.234
Could you think --
What would you --

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:18.234
-I mean I've --
Anything but what I said, no.

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:21.667
I've thought about it,
and there's a line --

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.400
"I've thought about it."
I'm such a dork.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.834
[ Laughter ]
There's a line in the movie

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:32.100
where John Hammond, the old man
who created Jurassic Park, says,

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.701
"Spared no expense."

00:02:33.701 --> 00:02:37.968
So, in hindsight, I wish
I gestured to the set,

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:40.033
which was kind of
an elaborate set --

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:42.000
it had, like, a staircase
and stuff --

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.400
and said, "Spared no expense."

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.767
-Oh, yeah. Spielberg comes out
and he goes, "I know that."

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:48.901
And you go --

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.033
-Wait, he's pointing at
my shirt.

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:51.501
-Yeah, okay, so --
-Go back, go back.

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:52.667
-Yeah, no problem.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:53.701
-Take two.

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:55.167
-How tall is Steven,
do you think?

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:57.067
-Um...
-You're standing or sitting?

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:59.000
-I'm standing. Should we stand?
-Let's re-create it.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.300
Let's re-create it.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.300
-I'm literally looking
like this.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.434
-Yep.
-And then --

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:06.634
-And I'm over here. And I go...

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:09.734
"Hey, I know that."

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:11.300
-"Spared no expense."

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:13.968 --> 00:03:15.934
-"You're gonna make it."
-"Thank you."

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.634
-"You're gonna make it."
-"Thank you."

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:18.901
-"You're gonna make it, kid.

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:21.033
I want you to be
in the next 10 movies."

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.434
-"Oh, I'm gonna be
in all your movies?"

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:25.033
-"The rest of my career."
-"Oh, my God, thank you."

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:26.434
-"I love you
and I love that attitude

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:28.000
and I love what you said."
-"Thank you.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.100
Did you say attitude and point
towards my waist area?"

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.567
[ Laughter ]
-"Yeah, I like your attitude."

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:34.634
-"I like your attitude."
-"I like your attitude."

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:36.901
[ Laughter ]
-"Thank you.

00:03:36.901 --> 00:03:38.400
Hey, man, I like your attitude."

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.834
-"Yeah, I like yours too."

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:43.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:45.534
-That's a new thing
people are doing.

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:47.767
"Hey, dude,
I like your attitude."

00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:49.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:51.901
Alright.
-"Thank my father, I guess."

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:55.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:58.200
-"Thank my father"?
-Why would you say that?

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:02.734
-"I had the weirdest experience
with Steven Spielberg.

00:04:02.734 --> 00:04:06.834
He said, 'I like your attitude,'

00:04:06.834 --> 00:04:09.367
and I said 'Thank my father.'"

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:11.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:14.334
"And now I'm still
in all of his movies."

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:16.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:18.167
Oh, my God.

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:20.033
-Yeah, an awkward, more awkward.

00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:22.334
-I know.
-Let's talk about your show.

00:04:22.334 --> 00:04:23.701
"Is It Cake?"
-Yes.

00:04:23.701 --> 00:04:25.133
-It's the number-one show.
Congratulations.

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:26.501
It's a big hit.
-Right. Thank you.

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:28.133
-On Netflix. "Is It Cake?"

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:30.634
People compete to see if they
can fake each other out.

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.834
And you have to slice it.

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:34.200
You're the deciding judge.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.000
You go, "Is it cake?"

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.234
-"Is it cake?"
-Yeah, and --

00:04:37.234 --> 00:04:39.601
[ Laughter ]
-It's really complicated.

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:42.834
-Well, here's why I would say,
you could argue that it could be

00:04:42.834 --> 00:04:45.300
a little nerve-wracking --
because if you mess up

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.767
the slice of the cake,

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:48.434
it's not like you have
10 of these cakes.

00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:50.367
They're pretty elaborate cakes.
-Right.

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:52.968
These bakers,
who are very talented,

00:04:52.968 --> 00:04:55.634
bake it for like eight hours,
I think.

00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:58.701
So they want the cut
to be right.

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:01.234
So, I have, like, an ear piece,

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:02.868
and they're like,
"Alright, here comes the cut."

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.767
-"Hey, here comes the cut.
Drum roll."

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:07.968
-And then you just have to
slice it right

00:05:07.968 --> 00:05:09.300
and, like, wedge it out.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.901
They're like, "This is
a standard cuttin' wedge, bud.

00:05:11.901 --> 00:05:13.767
You just want to cut it
and wedge it out."

00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:16.334
-But now you're an expert at
cake cutting.

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:19.567
-I mean, I'd think so, but I
got, like, a random message

00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:22.868
on Instagram that's like, "You
cut cake like an 8-year-old."

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:24.033
-Alright.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.033 --> 00:05:26.267
-I'm like,
"Well, that's all I have to do,

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:28.234
and I messed that up?"
-The Internet remains champion.

00:05:28.234 --> 00:05:30.300
-The Internet remains champion.
-It's undefeated.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.767
Yeah, yeah, undefeated.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:35.000
Here's Mikey Day hosting
"Is It Cake?"

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.234
Take a look at this.

00:05:36.234 --> 00:05:37.334
-Is it cake?

00:05:37.334 --> 00:05:38.601
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:05:38.601 --> 00:05:41.868
Ah. I'm just seeing where I want
to slice this here.

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:43.634
♪♪

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:44.567
[ Clink ]
-No!

00:05:44.567 --> 00:05:46.634
-Are you kidding?!

00:05:46.634 --> 00:05:47.734
-It's a conch!

00:05:47.734 --> 00:05:48.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.834 --> 00:05:50.501
-It's a conch.

00:05:50.501 --> 00:05:53.100
Andrew, it's not cake.
You did it, buddy.

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:56.100
You fooled the judges.
You're up for the win.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:06:00.133
-Thank you, guys. Thank you,
thank you, thank you.

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:02.234
-Kelly thought it was five.
Let's see.

00:06:02.234 --> 00:06:03.901
-I don't want to hear any noise.

00:06:03.901 --> 00:06:06.667
-Let's find out if this is cake.

00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:12.300
♪♪

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.367
-[ Gasps ]

00:06:13.367 --> 00:06:15.267
-Oh!
-Yes!

00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:19.033
Come on now! Come on now!

00:06:19.033 --> 00:06:20.701
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:25.200
-"Is It Cake?" is on Netflix
right now!

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.634
Mikey Day, everybody.

